{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unheedful-acceptable-fulmar","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\n\n`tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev.py::test_store_snapshot_survives_git_maintenance_but_still_catches_mutation` failed once in a full `make verify` (2026-11-11 00:20-00:50 PST, worktree fixver-epic at commit 4d21c744977, which does not touch bridge fsck). Line 254 `lock.unlink()` raised `FileNotFoundError` for `<tmp>/churn/.tickets-tracker/.git/objects/maintenance.lock`: the test wrote the file, `_store_snapshot` ran, and the file was gone before the test removed it. The same test passed 6 of 6 times run alone right afterwards. The earlier bug `chewed-illicit-blacklemur` (closed) described a race between this test and git auto-maintenance on macOS.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\n- A git process started inside the test fixture (auto-maintenance or gc) runs in the background and removes `objects/maintenance.lock` when it finishes.\n- The earlier fix narrowed the race but did not remove it; host load under `make verify` (4 xdist workers) widens it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction (for example, holding the background git process or forcing auto-maintenance in the fixture) shows the cause.\n- [ ] The test no longer depends on timing: the fixture disables git auto-maintenance/gc for its repos, or the test uses a lock path no git process deletes.\n- [ ] The test passes 200 consecutive runs under `pytest -n 4` load.","id":"422a-8867-4b6d-4900","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Recurrence: bridge fsck maintenance-lock test still races git maintenance under make verify"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794387176978229273,"uuid":"57ce35f3-96df-4384-9486-0b261f745ddc"}